  "worked_solution": "The interval of continuity of the vector-valued function is the intersection of the continuity intervals of all its components.\n\nLet's now consider the components of $f(t)$ one-by-one.\n\n- Function $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t$ is continuous for $t>0.$\n\n- Function $\\sqrt{t+1}$ is continuous for $t\\ge -1.$\n\n- Function ${t}^{3}-8$ is continuous for all real numbers.\n\nSo the interval of continuity for the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is the intersection of intervals $(0,\\infty )$  and $[-1,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the interval of continuity is $(0,\\infty ).$",
